---
const title = 'Yantra · WebGPU heat simulation in your browser';
---
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>{title}</title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
  <meta property="og:title" content="Yantra" />
  <meta property="og:description" content="WebGPU finite-element heat simulation, in a browser tab." />
  <style>
    :root { color-scheme: dark; }
    body { font: 16px/1.6 system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 4rem 1.5rem; background: #0b0b10; color: #e7e7ea; }
    h1 { font-size: 3.5rem; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
    h1 span { background: linear-gradient(120deg, #ff7a59, #fce459); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; background-clip: text; }
    p.lede { font-size: 1.2rem; color: #b9b9c2; margin: 0 0 2rem; }
    a.cta { display: inline-block; padding: 0.85rem 1.4rem; background: #fce459; color: #0b0b10; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 0.4rem; font-weight: 700; }
    .fixtures { margin-top: 3rem; }
    .fixtures a { display: block; padding: 1rem; margin: 0.5rem 0; background: #15151c; border-radius: 0.4rem; color: #e7e7ea; text-decoration: none; border: 1px solid #21212a; }
    .fixtures a:hover { background: #1c1c26; border-color: #2c2c38; }
    footer { margin-top: 4rem; color: #6a6a78; font-size: 0.85em; }
    code { background: #15151c; padding: 0.1em 0.35em; border-radius: 0.2rem; font-size: 0.9em; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1><span>Yantra.</span></h1>
  <p class="lede">Drop an STL. Set the hot side. Set the cold side. Watch heat conduct through the part — on your GPU, in your tab. No install. No cloud.</p>
  <a class="cta" href="/sim">Open simulator →</a>
  <div class="fixtures">
    <p>Or try a built-in fixture:</p>
    <a href="/sim?fx=cube">Cube (smoke test)</a>
    <a href="/sim?fx=sphere">Sphere</a>
    <a href="/sim?fx=fins">Finned heatsink</a>
  </div>
  <footer>Requires a WebGPU-capable browser (Chrome / Edge / Arc on 2026). Built with Astro · React · WebGPU · WGSL.</footer>
</body>
</html>
